# Headers Cloudflare adds to every file of the site (docs/stack.md, Hosting). The Vite dev and
# preview servers send the same ones, read from this file, so a page that breaks the policy
# breaks in development too.
#
# The policy, source by source:
#   script-src 'self'     the bundle only: no inline scripts, no eval. The JSON-LD block in
#                         index.html is data, which the policy doesn't govern.
#   'wasm-unsafe-eval'    compiling WebAssembly: the password key exchange in packages/crypto-wasm
#                         (the site's own module, fetched under connect-src 'self'). It allows no
#                         eval of JavaScript, and no script runs in Explorer's frame to use it.
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline'  Explorer's page frame inherits this policy, and pages are inline
#                         <style> and style attributes. No script can run in the frame, so a
#                         style can only change how a page looks.
#   img-src data:         avatars, icons in the stylesheet and the CRT's displacement map are
#                         data: images.
#   connect-src wss:      Nostr relays and Lighthouses can be at any host. ws: is for a
#                         Lighthouse on this computer; an https page can't open ws:// to any
#                         other host anyway, and a CSP can't name [::1].
#   frame-ancestors 'none' and X-Frame-Options  nobody may put Pigeon in a frame of theirs.
#   form-action 'none'    no form posts anywhere; the app handles every form itself.
#   Referrer-Policy       links out say nothing about where they came from.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' wss: ws:; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
